course: dictionary
lesson: 15938
title: Unsatisfactory: not good enough
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unsatisfactory means not good enough. Something is unsatisfactory when it does not meet what was wanted or needed. «Your spelling is unsatisfactory, so please practise it each night.» The teacher is not calling you a bad speller. She is saying your spelling is not yet good enough.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The repair was unsatisfactory: the tap still dripped.» A repair is meant to fix something. The tap still drips, so the repair did not do its job. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Not good enough fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: Unsatisfactory is a formal word, often found in school reports and inspections. Plainer words that mean the same are poor, disappointing or not good enough.
fact: Unsatisfactory means not good enough, not of the quality wanted.
fact: «Unsatisfactory» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «an unsatisfactory answer».
fact: The adverb is «unsatisfactorily», as in «The job was done unsatisfactorily».
fact: The opposite is satisfactory, which means good enough and meeting what was needed.
fact: Plain words for unsatisfactory are poor, disappointing and not good enough.
exercise: «The meal was unsatisfactory: cold soup and burnt toast.» What does unsatisfactory mean? | Full of fun | Huge and cheap | *Not good enough | Very tasty and warm
exercise: «Your report says your work is unsatisfactory.» Which plain word is closest in meaning? | Enormous | Quiet | *Poor | Brilliant
exercise: «The repair was unsatisfactory, so we asked the man to come back.» Why did they ask him to come back? | The man had forgotten his tools at home | *The repair was not good enough | They wanted a longer repair for the same price | The repair was perfect and they wanted to say thank you
test: Which word is the adverb form of unsatisfactory? | Unsatisfy | *Unsatisfactorily | Unsatisfactory | Satisfaction
test: «The team's effort was unsatisfactory, so the coach asked for more.» Which word could replace unsatisfactory? | Luminous | Excellent | *Poor | Ancient
exam: Which sentence uses unsatisfactory correctly? | *The sandwich was unsatisfactory: it was stale and soggy. | The sandwich was unsatisfactory: it was fresh, warm and tasty. | Unsatisfactory is the name of my dog's favourite toy.
